        "title": "Bacterial Disease",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nGRAM-POSITIVE:\n  Cytoplasm → Plasma membrane → Thick PG (20–80 nm) → surface proteins\n  Teichoic acids: interspersed in PG → facilitate biofilm, drug binding\n  Some have capsule (outer, polysaccharide) — antiphagocytic"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-BACTERIAL.md#009",
      "path": [
        "01-BACTERIAL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:disease:01-bacterial, git-history:disease:01-bacterial]",
        "canonical_path": "disease/01-BACTERIAL.md",
        "concepts": "[bacterial]",
        "current_path": "disease/01-BACTERIAL.md",
        "id": "maxim:disease:bacterial",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "disease",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[bacterial]",
        "section": "disease",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Bacterial Disease",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "GRAM-NEGATIVE:\n  Cytoplasm → Plasma membrane → Thin PG (2–7 nm) → Periplasm → Outer membrane\n  Outer membrane:\n    Inner leaflet: phospholipid\n    Outer leaflet: LPS (lipopolysaccharide)\n      Lipid A: embedded in OM, toxic endotoxin moiety — triggers TLR4 → TNF/IL-1 cascade → sepsis\n      Core polysaccharide: structural\n      O-antigen: highly variable polysaccharide chain → serotyping target (O antigen in E. coli O157:H7)\n  Porins (OmpC, OmpF): protein channels in OM for small molecule diffusion\n  Efflux pumps: span OM + PG + PM → pump out antibiotics\n```"
    },
