      "text": "### Virulence Factors"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-BACTERIAL.md#011",
      "path": [
        "01-BACTERIAL.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:disease:01-bacterial, git-history:disease:01-bacterial]",
        "canonical_path": "disease/01-BACTERIAL.md",
        "concepts": "[bacterial]",
        "current_path": "disease/01-BACTERIAL.md",
        "id": "maxim:disease:bacterial",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "disease",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[bacterial]",
        "section": "disease",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Bacterial Disease",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "| Factor | Mechanism | Examples |\n|--------|-----------|---------|\n| Capsule | Antiphagocytic (hides PAMPs from phagocyte PRRs) | S. pneumoniae, H. influenzae type b, N. meningitidis, K. pneumoniae |\n| Adhesins | Bind host cell receptors — required for colonization | Pili/fimbriae (UPEC mannose-binding type 1 pili → uroepithelium), M protein (GAS) |\n| Biofilm | Matrix-enclosed community; ↑↑ antibiotic resistance (~1,000×); immune evasion | S. epidermidis on catheters, P. aeruginosa in CF lungs, S. aureus on prosthetics |\n| Exotoxins | Protein toxins secreted by bacteria | See below |\n| Endotoxin (LPS) | Gram-negative OM component, not secreted; TLR4 agonist → cytokine storm | All gram-negatives; sepsis driver |\n| Superantigens | Bypass normal MHC/TCR specificity → massive T cell activation → cytokine storm | TSST-1 (S. aureus), SpeA (S. pyogenes) → toxic shock |\n| Siderophores | Iron chelators — compete for host iron (iron is limiting in host) | Enterobactin (E. coli), pyoverdine (Pseudomonas) |\n| Type III Secretion System (T3SS) | Molecular syringe — injects effector proteins directly into host cell cytoplasm | Salmonella (vacuole survival), Shigella (intracellular motility), EPEC (pedestal formation) |"
    },
