        "root_concepts": "[bacterial]",
        "section": "disease",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Bacterial Disease",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "BOTULINUM TOXIN (Clostridium botulinum):\n  A subunit: Zn²⁺-dependent protease → cleaves SNARE proteins (synaptobrevin/SNAP-25)\n  → ACh vesicles cannot fuse at NMJ → flaccid paralysis (descending, cranial nerves first)\n  Most potent toxin known (~1 ng/kg lethal)\n  Clinical use: therapeutic (cosmetic, dystonia, migraine, achalasia)"
    },
    {
